<description>&lt;p&gt;The rebuilt flood-damaged town is being promoted as a showcase for the Libyan strongman’s rule, while Fezzan revolutionaries are forcing contests against Haftar’s control in the south. The House of Representatives condemned Zintan’s obstruction of a parliamentary session and the armed closure of Zintan Airport, and the UN special representative welcomed amendments raising the recruitment age to 18. A white tiger cub was welcomed at the reopened Libyan zoo, and Libya’s oil reserves remain Africa’s largest yet Western majors are not investing. Combat intensity remains low, with 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTE1LNWtaVkVtaWR5blozTVduaVhRQXp2UEJhakxwMHhERGpxN2dxSmJzWnpRVktBWHllUWRGb1VacnZlTDFidGxCamNCUWNlQVdTZFpRRnVPM181aEE5TXc?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Crude Oil Prices Today | OilPrice.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxQcUVON1hneWlZM0ZQXzI2M3ljUHJlZlluYTFSOVRkenBVQXNNWEVJQkcwZ05Dcmc5NnlId1lZdWc1WmU4RnRqU29GRTJXcGVzTWQwZkp2VUlGQjlReEtsbFMySG53bHlJVm5mam52T0ZWbExZNmVQVTd2clBtZ2htLW9SWWFKUmg3VjFlN2xfek4wNGFEVmZicDNn?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Jamestown Foundation&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxPN2tRX3lhem9sQ3p2Rzh0OHRtVWp0b1FPSVRDMzR3bUx2TV9KV1Y3T1NkeUxJcGM1cUIzemMzc29pNTBDM0I3SUR1X29nakVfRF9Oa25LSHlETktjRkdMNWxYeTRKSjJFZHMycUJOblY5am9lQm4xQTk4cGJtZVZKelptRWY4UDZVZC1pbWZtcFdkeUk2VHNkaHd0TUk?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Libya Observer&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxORmF5NVExUU13N2dvVzJCcURfbFBleks4R25hVVE4aXYteU5qZXdCQlYxRXlnb0RnUG9VMWdwbi1ucWJrQTlFcXZKUzZveEpGcjRiVXNfQnQwN3FKTWlQMXpOX3JDSXlRY2VPRXVlNEdjOEo4eVNXNm5wX29qVi1CaHh4MUljc2o2QnJNNFhKbHZkV